{
  "version": 2,
  "why": "N1: replace polling with WebSockets on a dedicated gateway fleet behind a load balancer; a session registry (device → gateway) lets the chat service find the recipient's gateway; messages move to a wide-column store partitioned by conversation to absorb ~70k writes/s and 146 TB/year. Flaw left: the chat service delivers to every group member inline, so a 200-member group slows the sender and a slow gateway stalls the send.",
